From f4212e635f6d124c74e36a76556392df117601f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "suricata.lu" <suricata.lu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:47:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: chips-media: wave5: update min buffers after unlock in
 start_streaming

CIP patch 1802 (upstream 7d5d364f8b2d "media: chips-media: wave5: Fix
Reports from Kernel Lock Validator") moved the
V4L2_CID_MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_CAPTURE update out of
handle_dynamic_resolution_change(), which runs under the state spinlock,
into wave5_update_min_bufs_ctrl(), and made every upstream caller call
it after dropping the lock.

TI's 3e495a58f26a ("PENDING: media: chips-media: wave5: Parse Stream
Header During Start Stream on Output") adds one more caller in
wave5_vpu_dec_start_streaming(), a copy of the error path in
wave5_vpu_dec_device_run(). It is not upstream, so 1802 did not convert
it, and after 1802 that path no longer updates the control.

Convert it the same way 1802 converted the device_run() block: remember
inst->fbc_buf_count under the lock and call wave5_update_min_bufs_ctrl()
after the unlock.
---
 drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpu-dec.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpu-dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpu-dec.c
index 3c82906b50fb..80ba6450feaf 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpu-dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpu-dec.c
@@ -1553,6 +1553,7 @@ static int wave5_vpu_dec_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q, unsigned int count
 		ret = initialize_sequence(inst);
 		if (ret) {
 			unsigned long flags;
+			u32 fbc_buf_count = 0;
 
 			spin_lock_irqsave(&inst->state_spinlock, flags);
 			if (wave5_is_draining_or_eos(inst) &&
@@ -1561,14 +1562,18 @@ static int wave5_vpu_dec_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q, unsigned int count
 
 				switch_state(inst, VPU_INST_STATE_STOP);
 
-				if (vb2_is_streaming(dst_vq))
+				if (vb2_is_streaming(dst_vq)) {
 					send_eos_event(inst);
-				else
+				} else {
 					handle_dynamic_resolution_change(inst);
+					fbc_buf_count = inst->fbc_buf_count;
+				}
 
 				flag_last_buffer_done(inst);
 			}
 			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&inst->state_spinlock, flags);
+
+			wave5_update_min_bufs_ctrl(inst, fbc_buf_count);
 		} else {
 			switch_state(inst, VPU_INST_STATE_INIT_SEQ);
 		}
